WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
Two countries make the same product.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:06.580
In Country A, each worker
costs 50,000 a year.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.460
In Country B, each
worker costs just 20,000.

4
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.030
Surely B can sell more cheaply?

5
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.440
Yet the labour cost of
each unit is lower in A.

6
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.870
So what makes one country's goods
cheaper to buy than another's,

7
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.050
even when wages are higher?

8
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.000
In this mission, you'll
calculate unit labour costs,

9
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.600
and compare countries with their rivals.

10
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.770
Then you'll see what happened when
Spain's costs raced ahead of Germany's,

11
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.430
inside the euro.

12
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.370
Your mission: find out
what really sets the cost

13
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.800
of what a country sells.
